  "details": "**Summary**\nController buttons cannot be pressed when the corresponding controller loses tracking. A loss of tracking should not prevent players from using the buttons or control stick.\n**Details**\nI'm using a Valve Index and SteamVR, though this issue might occur on other platforms as well.\n\nOccasionally my controllers lose tracking for several - i. e. after leaving the SteamVR menu or after accidently occluding a controller.\n\nThis causes VRChat (and SteamVR) to stop tracking the controller. Which makes sense.\n\nBut VRChat also prevents that controller from issuing any inputs, even though it's still connected. Which prevents us from using the thumbstick to move, or using a button to unmute ourselves. \n\nI'm not sure whether there's a valid reason for this, but I think it makes VRChat more difficult to use.\n\n**Proposed fix**\nOnly disable a controller's input if it is disconnected. Keep a controller's input enabled, even on tracking loss.",
